{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '150,180p' docs/design/dao.lease.md; rg -n \\\"classify-entry|unknown|tolerance|resumed\\\" src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"4. **Classify.** A lease is due for reclaim when any of these holds, and the\n   first that holds in this order is its cause: it is already `pending`, and\n   keeps the cause it carries; a valid `:released` from its holder has been\n   observed, `:release`; its tenure start is further back than\n   `:dao.lease/max`, `:cap`; the grantor's own policy ends it, `:policy`; its\n   interval since the last relevant observation exceeds duration plus\n   tolerance, `:silence`. A lease whose evidence state is `unknown` is due for\n   `:silence` only once a full duration has passed since its resumed reading.\n5. **Reclaim** each due lease by its composition-supplied procedure, marking it\n   `pending` with its cause first. The procedure is idempotent and reports\n   whether it succeeded; a reclaim that fails or does not report leaves the\n   lease `pending` and unrecorded.\n6. **Record** `:lapsed`, carrying the cause the ledger holds, for each lease\n   whose reclaim succeeded. On `:dao.stream/ok` the lease leaves the ledger;\n   otherwise it stays `pending` and the next pass reaches it again through the\n   first clause of step 4.\n\nThe record follows the act and never precedes it. **The absence of a `:lapsed`\nfact is never evidence of tenure.**\n\nA drain that ends in `:dao.stream/end` retires that cursor for subsequent\npasses. A drain that ends in `:dao.stream/transport-error` ends the pass before\nstep 4.\n\n### Judging with incomplete evidence\n\nAbsence is evidence only over a window the judge observed. After a\n`:dao.stream/gap`, a lease with no renewal in the retained tail is `unknown`,\nand a surviving older renewal is not inferred to be the newest. A lease\nrecovered from a persisted ledger is `unknown`. Conditions other than\n`:silence` apply to an `unknown` lease unchanged.\n55:  \"Upper bound on a duration's base magnitude: 2^52. `duration?`/`tolerance?`\n95:(defn tolerance?\n96:  \"duration? permitting a zero magnitude, as a judge's tolerance may be zero.\"\n347:    [:unknown-status]))\n363:    [:unknown-event]))\n626:  :tolerance     a duration map, possibly zero; nil means zero\n662:        tolerance (get config :tolerance)\n675:    ;; result for an unknown source or a missing envelope key -- read as\n682:    ;; A tolerance in a unit the table does not know -- or past the unit's\n686:    (when (some? tolerance)\n687:      (check-assembly! (tolerance? tolerance)\n688:                       \"the tolerance is a single-entry {unit non-negative-integer} map within the bound\"\n689:                       {:tolerance tolerance :refused :tolerance})\n690:      (let [unit (first (keys tolerance))\n691:            magnitude (get tolerance unit)]\n693:                         \"the tolerance's unit is in the unit table\"\n694:                         {:tolerance tolerance :units units :refused :tolerance})\n697:                         \"the tolerance's magnitude is within the per-unit bound\"\n698:                         {:tolerance tolerance :units units :refused :tolerance})))\n700:     :tolerance tolerance\n737:  facts it observes there, and marks exactly those unknown when that medium\n862:  pass late, not wrong, and marks nothing unknown: resume from the recovery\n1041:(defn- mark-medium-unknown\n1043:  authoritatively observed -- and only that medium's -- unknown, with now as\n1044:  its resumed reading; a surviving older renewal is not inferred to be the\n1045:  newest, so unknown is the state whatever the retained tail holds.\n1052:  Conditions other than :silence apply to an unknown lease unchanged.\"\n1061:                                 :evidence :unknown\n1062:                                 :resumed (:now judge)))\n1149:                judge' (mark-medium-unknown judge entry)]\n1290:(defn- duration-plus-tolerance\n1291:  [units duration tolerance]\n1292:  (if (nil? tolerance) duration (add-duration units duration tolerance)))\n1304:  carry, registered or not, :unknown.) Suppression is sound against\n1325:(defn- classify-entry\n1332:  plus tolerance, in silence. A lease whose evidence is unknown is due for\n1333:  :silence only once a full duration has passed since its resumed reading;\n1335:  :silence clauses only (see `silence-suppressed`), and an unknown entry\n1336:  with no resumed reading is never due for silence -- there is no window to\n1358:           (= :unknown (:evidence entry))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
